SUMMARY:Art Loeb at BRP to Pilot Mtn - 6.3 Mi\, 1900 Ft EG
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Details**\n\n* 6 Miles\, 2000 Ft
  elevation gain\n* Carpool meeting time is 8:30 at the Asheville Outlets p
 arking lot behind the Waffle House.\n* Sign up starts Friday at 8pm\n\nThi
 s is a nice out and back along the Art Loeb trail to Pilot Mountain which 
 has a beautiful view at the turn around. Some of the trail is a bit overgr
 own although not bad but I recommend long pants. **Although the distance a
 nd elevation might sound like a moderate hike\, most of the elevation gain
  comes in the last 1.5 miles. It felt like a much harder hike when I scout
 ed because of that so please don't sign up unless you are okay for a chall
 enge at the end with no way to go but up**.\n\nI enjoy stopping at the Pis
 gah Inn after the hike and sitting in the rocking chairs behind the hotel.
  They have a convenience store where you can buy drinks and sandwiches or 
 you can bring your own. We will try to break up into cars that want to do 
 that and want to just go back to the carpool area.\n\nhttps://www.alltrail
 s.com/explore/custom-routes/uploaded-route-72e4032\n\n**CARPOOL**\nWe will
  meet at the Asheville Outlets behind the Waffle House at 8:30. It is abou
 t a 50 minute ride to the trailhead. Please be there a little early so we 
 can leave at 8:30 for the trailhead. There is very limited parking at the 
 trailhead and it is all along the side of the road. If you plan to meet us
  at the trailhead\, plan to be there by 9:15. See the AllTrails link below
  for directions to the trailhead.\n\n**WEATHER**\nI'll watch the weather a
 nd post a cancellation message by 7:00 AM if the forecast is >50% chance o
 f precipitation.\n\n**QUESTIONS?**\nYou can message me through MeetUp unti
 l 9:00 AM the day of. Cell reception may be sketchy\, but you can try to t
 ext or call me up to the start of the hike: (508) 965-2333.\n\n**LEGALESE*
 *\nThis Asheville Hiking Group event involves hiking and\, possibly\, tran
 sportation to and from the meetup site. Participants are responsible for t
 heir own safety and affirm that they have the appropriate skills\, physica
 l conditioning\, equipment\, and supplies. Hiking may involve risks to one
 self and property. Neither your hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking Group 
 can assure your safety nor eliminate all risks. Participants assume full r
 esponsibility for any injuries\, damages\, or losses.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/315412182
 /
