SUMMARY:Scenic AVL #3:  Kennilworth
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nThis route includes the Kenilworth
  neighborhood and the historically diverse South Asheville neighborhood. W
 e will stop at a historic church and cemetery\, as well as Kenilworth Park
  and Chiles House. We will go up Reservoir Rd to take in the view and get 
 a workout.\n\n**Rating: Moderate+**\n**Distance:** 5 miles\n**Elevation:**
  670 feet\n**Surface:** Road\n**Type:** Butterfly Loop\n**Pace:** 3 mph on
  the flats\, slower up Reservoir Rd\n**Gear:** In winter\, please bring a 
 headlamp or flashlight. water\, snack\, poles for the climb\n**Features:**
  Neighborhood charm Kenilworth\, a little history\, and views from the top
 . Not likely to see bears - but we did see one near this route earlier in 
 the spring.\n**Dogs:** On leash.\n**Cautions:** Maintain normal traffic aw
 areness.\n**Route:** [Kenilworth to Reservoir Rd ](https://www.alltrails.c
 om/explore/map/kenilworth-to-reservoir-road-overlook-d9e74f4?p=-1&sh=ifwm3
 x).\n\n**Scenic Asheville Series:** There are 9 [hikes](https://docs.googl
 e.com/document/d/11ewlUM9OV8I4npc1cNNsSYOnXI0QPw2isAleXdFzEbI/edit?usp=dri
 vesdk) in the series\; hike them all and receive an [attractive badge](htt
 ps://docs.google.com/drawings/d/1goXUXfzUBqhB4_UeCxodlk4ZPeCCgqZrWK2EUJvk_
 vI/edit) for your backpack. Badgers can always attend hikes\, even if you 
 are on the waiting list\n\n**On-Time Departure**\nI typically have 1 or 2 
 no-shows on my hikes\, so we don't wait for people to arrive.\n\nIf you ar
 e late\, park on Chile's Avenue near [Leah Chile's Park](https://maps.app.
 goo.gl/ZUs81uHukoRMWQuP8?g_st=ac)\nand meet us at the historical marker at
  the top of the park across from Chile's house.\n\n**Guests and Plus Ones*
 *\nThis is a pretty good hike to bring guests. It is not as tough as some 
 of the hikes in the series\, and if someone wants to bail after the first 
 loop\, it is easy to find your way back to the cars.\n\n**Disclaimer and R
 elease of Liability:**\nThis activity involves hiking on city streets that
  may have traffic. Participants are responsible for their safety on street
 s and trails. The organizer of this trip is a volunteer and not a professi
 onal guide. The function of the organizer is only to organize this trip. I
 f you sign up or participate in this event you acknowledge that you freely
  and voluntarily agree to assume all risks of injuries\, illnesses\, and d
 amages arising from\, as a result of\, and associated with this event. In 
 addition\, you acknowledge that you agree to the Meetup terms: [https://ww
 w.meetup.com/terms](https://www.meetup.com/terms)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/315418161
 /
