SUMMARY:Chestnut Cove--Pine Mountain loops  8 miles 1300' ascent
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Details**: This is a double loop
  hike along the MST from Chestnut Cove Overlook to Pine Mountain and back.
  This is a beautiful and quiet section of the MST. Good Footing. Shaded. P
 ace 2.4 mph. About 8 miles and under 1300' ascent. Most of the elevation g
 ain is in the first half of the hike. Max Elevation: 4\,000'. Well behaved
  dogs on a leash are OK.\n**After the hike\, get together at the Stoneridg
 e Tavern for a beverage and/or lunch.**\n**Tailhead**: Chestnut Cove Overl
 ook\, Blue Ridge Pkwy\n**How to find us:** Directions from I-26\, exit 33 
 (Blue Ridge Parkway\, Brevard Rd) South on Brevard Rd (NC-191) for 2.4 mil
 es to the light at the Arboretum / BRP entrance. Turn Right (South) on the
  Blue Ridge Parkway to Chestnut Cove Overlook (about 5 miles) Prompt 8:30 
 AM departure\nNote: If the hike has to be cancelled due to weather\, this 
 will be done by 7AM on the day of the hike---look for notification on-line
 \n\n\\*\\***Courtesy** (Please read carefully!)\\*\\* Only sign up if you 
 \\\\\\*truly\\\\\\* plan to come. If you must cancel\, please change your 
 status to "Not Going" as soon as possible. Avoid dropping out within 24 ho
 urs of the hike so that wait-listers can have sufficient notice. And pleas
 e please PLEASE don't be a no-show\n**LEGALESE**\nThis Asheville Hiking Gr
 oup event involves hiking and\, possibly\, transportation to and from the 
 meetup site. Participants are responsible for their own safety and affirm 
 that they have the appropriate skills\, physical conditioning\, equipment\
 , and supplies. Hiking may involve risks to oneself and property. Neither 
 your hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking Group can assure your safety nor 
 eliminate all risks. Participants assume full responsibility for any injur
 ies\, damages\, or losses.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/315410305
 /
